  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Activity 1.1 

- Tender documentation prepared
- EPC contractor selected, contracted
- Social and environmental impact permit successfully obtained, and SES strategy approved
- Electricity Power generation and distribution licenses successfully obtained

Activity 1.2
- PV power plant installed 
- Battery storage system installed
- Number of step up/down transformers installed
- MV line to distribute power from PV power plant to the RFM Hospital main switchboard constructed and installed

Activity 1.3
- Number of high energy bulbs and fittings replaced with LEDs lamps 
- Old electric heaters replaced with high efficiency heat pumps
- Coal boiler replacement with high efficiency heat pumps

Activity 2.1
- A baseline of energy consumption prior to the installation of energy efficient appliances and devices and the PV power plant and a baseline of energy costs established
-Indicators for monitoring energy consumption and associated costs and greenhouse gas emission levels selected
- Monitoring system to track and document emission trends, energy demand levels and energy costs at the RFM Hospital designed and implemented
- System for monitoring and reporting of data on energy consumption and costs and Greenhouse gas emissions particularly CO2 emissions put in place
 
Activity 2.2
- Lessons and good practices from the implementation of the project and the key lessons and experiences captured and documented 
- Media of knowledge sharing to the key stakeholders established
- Knowledge products on the cost-benefits of using renewable energy technologies / systems and efficient appliances and share among public and private sector relevant stakeholders using different multi-media channels produced
- On-the-job and formal training for local professionals and expertise from public and private sectors on use of renewable energy and energy efficient systems by encouraging the contractor to engage local people in the implementation greening activities put in place
- A case study a</narrative>
    </description>
